<article class="env-example" id="056A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/056A">Example <span data-tag="056A">29.6.4</span>.</a> If $A \to B$ is a ring map with kernel $I$, then the scheme theoretic image of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is the closed subscheme $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A/I)$ of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01R8" data-tag="01R8">29.6.3</a>. </p>
